              ":question/id": "cbf28a0c-c34d-5855-b72e-4225a11710c1",
              ":question/math-academy-id": "e-13129",
              ":question/problem": "Consider the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x+2y &=8 \\\\ 2x-y &=6\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nUse the diagram below to determine this system's solution $(x,y)$.\n\n![](images/6f/6f0b7960b9b4c98250741b009da2ad19c1123c5b7adf9cd5072430fb9a879dc9.png)",
              ":question/worked-solution": "The solution of the system corresponds to the point of intersection of the lines. \n\n![](images/5c/5c1c69adc880ea7cfdb5a4e0a10abd6032d2eedf0386923b94df9b7c173edd6d.png)\n\nIn this case, we have the point $(4,2).$ Therefore, the solution to the given system is $(4,2).$"
            },
